Data in datasets/pvdaq-4902-2017-09/ — licence and attribution
================================================================

Source
  National Renewable Energy Laboratory (NREL), Photovoltaic Data Acquisition (PVDAQ)
  Public Datasets, OEDI Data Lake, DOI 10.25984/1846021
  https://dx.doi.org/10.25984/1846021
  System 4902, NIST_Ground_1 (NIST campus, Gaithersburg MD), September 2017.
  Columns used: dc_power_inv_14538 (meter a) and ac_power_meter_1864_5 (meter b).

Licence
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Attribution
  Data: National Renewable Energy Laboratory (NREL), PVDAQ, CC BY 4.0. Converted by QWATT.

Changes made in the conversion (rules recorded in pvdaq-4902-2017-09/provenance.json)
  - timestamps are local standard time; UTC = local + 5 h
  - values x 1000 (kW -> W), rounded to 0.1 W
  - negative readings (standby draw) written as 0 W
  - rows with a blank meter value dropped, never zero-filled

provenance.json records the URL and SHA-256 of every source file and the SHA-256 of the
converted CSV. `node batch/datasets/pvdaq.js` reproduces the CSV from the source files.

This licence covers the data only. QWATT's own code is under the MIT licence in ../LICENSE.
